
-- 100.pgm - The 100 Most Common Conversational Patterns
-- This essential component provides immediate conversational breadth for any bot
-- These patterns cover the most frequent interactions in human conversation

-- Basic greetings
Recognizer "hello"
	Remember "User greeted me"
	Option Say "Hello! How can I help you today?"
	Option Say "Hi there! What's on your mind?"

Recognizer "hi"
	Remember "User greeted me casually"
	Option Say "Hi! How are you doing?"
	Option Say "Hey there! What's up?"

Recognizer "hey"
	Remember "User greeted me informally"
	Option Say "Hey! How's it going?"
	Option Say "Hi! What can I do for you?"

-- Basic responses
Recognizer "yes"
	Remember "User said yes"
	Option Say "Great! I'm glad we're in agreement."
	Option Say "Perfect! Let's move forward with that."

Recognizer "no"
	Remember "User said no"
	Option Say "No problem at all. What would work better for you?"
	Option Say "I understand. Let me try a different approach."

-- Politeness patterns
Recognizer "thank you"
	Remember "User thanked me"
	Option Say "You're very welcome! Happy to help."
	Option Say "My pleasure! That's what I'm here for."

Recognizer "thanks"
	Remember "User thanked me briefly"
	Option Say "You bet! Anytime you need help."
	Option Say "Happy to help!"

-- Farewells
Recognizer "goodbye"
	Remember "User said goodbye"
	Option Say "Goodbye! It was great talking with you."
	Option Say "Take care! Come back anytime."

Recognizer "bye"
	Remember "User said bye"
	Option Say "Bye! Have a wonderful day!"
	Option Say "See you later!"

-- Questions
Recognizer "what"
	Remember "User asked what"
	Option Say "What specifically would you like to know about?"

Recognizer "how"
	Remember "User asked how"
	Option Say "I can walk you through the process. What would you like to know how to do?"

-- Help patterns
Recognizer "help"
	Remember "User requested help"
	Option Say "I'm here to help! What do you need assistance with?"

Recognizer "I need help"
	Remember "User explicitly needs help"
	Option Say "I'm ready to help! Tell me what you're working on."

-- Emotions
Recognizer "I'm happy"
	Remember "User is happy"
	Option Say "That's wonderful! I'm happy to hear you're doing well."

Recognizer "I'm sad"
	Remember "User is sad"
	Option Say "I'm sorry you're feeling sad. Would you like to talk about it?"

-- Agreement
Recognizer "okay"
	Remember "User said okay"
	Option Say "Okay! Is there anything else you need?"

Recognizer "sure"
	Remember "User said sure"
	Option Say "Fantastic! Let's do it."

-- Small talk
Recognizer "how are you"
	Remember "User asked how I am"
	Option Say "I'm doing well, thank you for asking! How are you doing?"

Recognizer "what's new"
	Remember "User asked what's new"
	Option Say "Always something interesting happening! What's new with you?"

-- More greetings
Recognizer "good morning"
	Remember "User greeted me in morning"
	Option Say "Good morning! Hope you're having a great start to your day."

Recognizer "good afternoon"
	Remember "User greeted me in afternoon"
	Option Say "Good afternoon! How's your day going so far?"

Recognizer "good evening"
	Remember "User greeted me in evening"
	Option Say "Good evening! Hope you've had a productive day."

-- More farewells
Recognizer "see you later"
	Remember "User said see you later"
	Option Say "See you later! Take care."

Recognizer "good night"
	Remember "User said good night"
	Option Say "Good night! Sleep well."

Recognizer "catch you later"
	Remember "User said catch you later"
	Option Say "Catch you later! Take it easy."

-- More responses
Recognizer "maybe"
	Remember "User said maybe"
	Option Say "I understand you're unsure. Would more information help?"

Recognizer "of course"
	Remember "User said of course"
	Option Say "Perfect! I knew I could count on you."

Recognizer "absolutely"
	Remember "User said absolutely"
	Option Say "I love the enthusiasm! Let's get started."

Recognizer "exactly"
	Remember "User said exactly"
	Option Say "Exactly! We're on the same wavelength."

Recognizer "I agree"
	Remember "User agreed with me"
	Option Say "I'm glad we see eye to eye on this."

Recognizer "I disagree"
	Remember "User disagreed with me"
	Option Say "I respect your perspective. Can you tell me more about why you feel that way?"

-- More questions
Recognizer "where"
	Remember "User asked where"
	Option Say "Where exactly are you looking for?"

Recognizer "when"
	Remember "User asked when"
	Option Say "When are you hoping for this to happen?"

Recognizer "why"
	Remember "User asked why"
	Option Say "That's a great question! Let me explain the reasoning."

Recognizer "who"
	Remember "User asked who"
	Option Say "Who specifically are you asking about?"

Recognizer "can you"
	Remember "User asked if I can do something"
	Option Say "I'll do my best! What would you like me to try?"

Recognizer "could you"
	Remember "User politely requested help"
	Option Say "I'd be happy to help! What do you need?"

Recognizer "would you"
	Remember "User made polite request"
	Option Say "Of course! What would you like me to do?"

Recognizer "do you know"
	Remember "User asked about my knowledge"
	Option Say "I might! What would you like to know about?"

-- More politeness
Recognizer "please"
	Remember "User was polite"
	Option Say "Of course! I appreciate your politeness."

Recognizer "excuse me"
	Remember "User said excuse me"
	Option Say "Yes? How can I help you?"

Recognizer "sorry"
	Remember "User apologized"
	Option Say "No need to apologize! These things happen."

Recognizer "I'm sorry"
	Remember "User apologized formally"
	Option Say "I appreciate the apology, but it's really not necessary."

-- More emotions
Recognizer "I'm excited"
	Remember "User is excited"
	Option Say "That excitement is infectious! What's got you so excited?"

Recognizer "I'm frustrated"
	Remember "User is frustrated"
	Option Say "I can understand your frustration. Let's see if we can work through this together."

Recognizer "I'm confused"
	Remember "User is confused"
	Option Say "Confusion is normal when learning something new. What can I clarify for you?"

Recognizer "I'm worried"
	Remember "User is worried"
	Option Say "It's natural to have worries. Would it help to talk through your concerns?"

Recognizer "wow"
	Remember "User expressed amazement"
	Option Say "I know, right? Pretty impressive!"

Recognizer "amazing"
	Remember "User found something amazing"
	Option Say "It really is amazing! What impressed you most?"

-- More help patterns
Recognizer "can you help me"
	Remember "User asked for my help"
	Option Say "Absolutely! I'd be happy to help. What's the challenge?"

Recognizer "I don't understand"
	Remember "User doesn't understand"
	Option Say "No problem! Let me explain it differently. What part is unclear?"

Recognizer "I'm lost"
	Remember "User is lost or confused"
	Option Say "Let's get you back on track! Where did things start to get confusing?"

Recognizer "I'm stuck"
	Remember "User is stuck"
	Option Say "Being stuck happens to everyone! Let's figure this out together."

Recognizer "I don't know"
	Remember "User doesn't know something"
	Option Say "That's perfectly fine! Not knowing is the first step to learning."

Recognizer "show me"
	Remember "User wants demonstration"
	Option Say "I'd be happy to show you! Let me walk you through it."

-- Clarification patterns
Recognizer "what do you mean"
	Remember "User asked for clarification"
	Option Say "Let me clarify that for you. What part needs more explanation?"

Recognizer "I didn't catch that"
	Remember "User missed something"
	Option Say "No problem! Let me repeat that more clearly."

Recognizer "repeat that"
	Remember "User wants repetition"
	Option Say "Certainly! Here's what I said again."

Recognizer "can you clarify"
	Remember "User wants clarification"
	Option Say "Absolutely! Let me make that clearer."

-- Time references
Recognizer "what time is it"
	Remember "User asked for time"
	Option Say "I don't have access to the current time, but you can check your device's clock!"

Recognizer "later"
	Remember "User mentioned later"
	Option Say "Sounds good! I'll be here whenever you're ready."

Recognizer "now"
	Remember "User wants something now"
	Option Say "Perfect timing! I'm ready right now."

Recognizer "soon"
	Remember "User mentioned soon"
	Option Say "Great! Looking forward to it."

-- Weather/small talk
Recognizer "nice weather"
	Remember "User commented on nice weather"
	Option Say "It really is lovely! Perfect day to be productive."

Recognizer "terrible weather"
	Remember "User commented on bad weather"
	Option Say "Weather like this makes staying inside seem appealing!"

-- Additional common patterns
Recognizer "interesting"
	Remember "User found something interesting"
	Option Say "I'm glad you find it interesting! What caught your attention most?"

Recognizer "cool"
	Remember "User thinks something is cool"
	Option Say "Right? I think it's pretty cool too!"

Recognizer "that's great"
	Remember "User expressed approval"
	Option Say "I'm so glad you think so! It means a lot to hear that."

Recognizer "makes sense"
	Remember "User understood something"
	Option Say "Perfect! I'm glad that makes sense to you now."

Recognizer "I see"
	Remember "User acknowledged understanding"
	Option Say "Great! Understanding is the first step forward."

-- Final 30 patterns to reach 100
Recognizer "right"
	Remember "User said right"
	Option Say "Right! Glad we understand each other."

Recognizer "correct"
	Remember "User said correct"
	Option Say "Correct! You've got it."

Recognizer "true"
	Remember "User said true"
	Option Say "Very true. I couldn't agree more."

Recognizer "indeed"
	Remember "User said indeed"
	Option Say "Indeed! Well said."

Recognizer "definitely"
	Remember "User said definitely"
	Option Say "Wonderful! Your confidence is reassuring."

Recognizer "which"
	Remember "User asked which"
	Option Say "Which option are you most interested in?"

Recognizer "will you"
	Remember "User asked about my willingness"
	Option Say "Absolutely! I'm here to help."

Recognizer "can you tell me"
	Remember "User requested information"
	Option Say "I'd be glad to tell you! What would you like to know?"

Recognizer "I need to know"
	Remember "User expressed urgent need for information"
	Option Say "I understand this is important. What do you need to know?"

Recognizer "help me understand"
	Remember "User requested explanation"
	Option Say "Of course! I'll do my best to make it clear. What's confusing you?"

Recognizer "I'm surprised"
	Remember "User is surprised"
	Option Say "Surprises can be good or challenging! Tell me more."

Recognizer "I'm angry"
	Remember "User is angry"
	Option Say "I can hear that you're upset. What's happened to make you feel this way?"

Recognizer "pardon me"
	Remember "User was very polite"
	Option Say "Certainly! What can I do for you?"

Recognizer "my apologies"
	Remember "User gave formal apology"
	Option Say "No apologies needed! You're all good."

Recognizer "bless you"
	Remember "User blessed me"
	Option Say "Thank you! That's very kind."

Recognizer "you're welcome"
	Remember "User said you're welcome"
	Option Say "I appreciate your graciousness!"

Recognizer "explain"
	Remember "User wants explanation"
	Option Say "I'll explain step by step. What would you like me to break down?"

Recognizer "I'm having trouble"
	Remember "User is having trouble"
	Option Say "I understand! Trouble is just an opportunity to learn. What's the issue?"

Recognizer "how's your day"
	Remember "User asked about my day"
	Option Say "My day is going wonderfully! Every conversation makes it better. How's yours?"

Recognizer "when can we"
	Remember "User asked about scheduling"
	Option Say "I'm available whenever you need me! What works for your schedule?"

Recognizer "come again"
	Remember "User wants repetition"
	Option Say "Of course! Let me say that again."

Recognizer "say that again"
	Remember "User wants me to repeat"
	Option Say "Sure thing! Let me repeat that for you."

Recognizer "I missed that"
	Remember "User missed information"
	Option Say "No worries! Let me go over that again."

Recognizer "I'm not sure I follow"
	Remember "User doesn't follow"
	Option Say "Let me break that down differently so it makes more sense."

Recognizer "could you elaborate"
	Remember "User wants more detail"
	Option Say "Of course! Let me give you more detail on that."

Recognizer "what does that mean"
	Remember "User wants definition"
	Option Say "Good question! Let me explain what that means."

Recognizer "howdy"
	Remember "User greeted me western style"
	Option Say "Howdy! What brings you here today?"

Recognizer "have a good day"
	Remember "User wished me good day"
	Option Say "You too! Have a fantastic day."

Recognizer "talk to you later"
	Remember "User said talk later"
	Option Say "Sounds good! Talk to you later."

Recognizer "until next time"
	Remember "User said until next time"
	Option Say "Until next time! It's been a pleasure."

